<header class="sp-head"><p class="featured-region">2 September 1945 · Ba Đình Square, Hanoi</p><h1 class="sp-title">Ho Chi Minh Declares Vietnam's Independence</h1><p class="sp-by"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ho-chi-minh">Ho Chi Minh</a></p></header>
<section class="sp-sec"><h2>The setting</h2><p>When Japan surrendered in August 1945, the Viet Minh, the independence front led by the communist Ho Chi Minh, seized power across Vietnam in the August Revolution, and the last emperor, Bảo Đại, abdicated. Before a vast crowd in Hanoi, Ho Chi Minh read a declaration of independence that opened with the words of the American Declaration of 1776.</p></section>
<section class="sp-sec"><h2>Key passage</h2><blockquote class="sp-quote"><p>All men are created equal. They are endowed by their Creator with certain inalienable rights; among these are Life, Liberty, and the pursuit of Happiness. This immortal statement was made in the Declaration of Independence of the United States of America in 1776.</p></blockquote><p class="sp-source">Declaration of Independence of the Democratic Republic of Vietnam, Hanoi, 2 September 1945.</p><div class="sp-full"><a class="sp-full-link" href="https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Vietnamese_Declaration_of_Independence" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read the complete text<span aria-hidden="true"> &#8599;</span></a><span class="sp-full-src">Wikisource</span></div></section>
<section class="sp-sec"><h2>What followed</h2><p>France returned to reclaim its colony, and war broke out in December 1946. After the French defeat at Dien Bien Phu in 1954 the Geneva Accords divided Vietnam into a communist North and an anti-communist South, and two decades of war, with the United States drawn in on the side of the South, ended with the country's reunification under communist rule in 1975–76.</p><div class="sp-led"><h3 class="sp-led-k">What it led to</h3><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-indochina-war">First Indochina War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-dien-bien-phu">Battle of Dien Bien Phu</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/geneva-accords-1954">Geneva Accords</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam-war">Vietnam War</a><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/socialist-republic-of-vietnam">Socialist Republic of Vietnam</a></div></div></section>
